# Template Library Architecture

The uploaded master CV is a **content source only** — its own visual layout
is never preserved or edited. Instead, the app ships a small, fixed library
of hand-built HTML/CSS resume templates that the user picks from in the
frontend gallery (`TemplateGallery.tsx`). This is implemented as:

1. `app/services/cv_structurer.py` (+ `docx_segmenter.py`) — parses the
   master CV's *content* (contact, summary, skills, per-job title/company/
   dates/bullets, education) into `MasterCvData`. Layout/formatting of the
   original document is irrelevant past this step.
2. `app/db/models.py`'s `ResumeTemplate` — one row per selectable template,
   seeded from `app/templates/resumes/<slug>/` folders by
   `app/services/template_registry.seed_templates_from_disk` on startup.
   Each folder holds `template.html.jinja2` (the layout) and `reference.pdf`
   (the original sample CV the design is modeled on — its first page is
   rasterized via PyMuPDF into the gallery thumbnail, so the picker shows
   the real sample, never a synthetic re-render).
3. `app/services/template_renderer.py` — fills the selected template's
   Jinja2 file with the AI-tailored `TailoredResumeContent`, then renders
   that HTML to PDF via a warm, shared Playwright Chromium instance
   (started/stopped in `app/main.py`'s lifespan).
4. DOCX output is derived from the *rendered PDF*, not a second hand-built
   renderer: `app/services/docx_to_pdf.convert_to_docx` (Word COM) opens the
   PDF and `SaveAs2`s it as `.docx` — the same conversion helper already
   used elsewhere in this file, reused as-is.

# Adding or editing a template

Every template folder needs exactly `template.html.jinja2` + `reference.pdf`.
The Jinja2 file receives one variable, `resume` (a `TailoredResumeContent` —
see `app/models/schemas.py`), and must render every field-bearing section
(contact, summary, skills, experience, education, certifications, languages)
so no tailored content is silently dropped for any real resume. Register the
new slug's display name/description in
`template_registry.py`'s `_TEMPLATE_META` dict. Do not add a new
template outside the folders already seeded from sample CVs without an
explicit request.

# The fixed bullet count exception

Every experience entry must end up with exactly `EXPERIENCE_BULLET_COUNT`
(see `app/core/constants.py`) bullets, fully regenerated to target the JD —
**not** matched to the master CV's own original per-job bullet count. Every
template's experience section must render however many bullets
`ExperienceEntry.bullets` actually contains (a plain `{% for %}` loop) —
never hardcode a bullet count or truncate/pad in the template itself; that
padding/trimming already happened in `ai_tailor._assemble_full_resume`
before the resume ever reaches the renderer.

# Rendering failure handling

`template_renderer.render_pdf` returns `None` (never raises) if the shared
Chromium instance isn't running (e.g. `playwright install chromium` was
never run) — `download_resume` in `backend/app/api/routes/resume.py` turns
that into a clear 500 error rather than a silent blank download. DOCX
conversion failures (Word COM unavailable) are surfaced the same way, only
when `format=docx` was actually requested.
